{#
	Hero image

	The masthead is the largest contentful paint of every public page, so the
	photo behind it is preloaded per breakpoint and handed to styles.css as the
	--masthead-image-{small,medium,wide,large} custom properties. The media
	queries here have to be the ones styles.css switches on, or the browser
	preloads a picture it never paints.

	Those boundaries are 640 / 1280 / 1920, which are the widths of the
	variants themselves and not Bootstrap's breakpoints. `.masthead` is
	`width: 100%` with `background-size: cover`, so a variant narrower than its
	viewport range gets stretched by the browser; the boundaries therefore have
	to be the variant widths. At 768/1920 as they used to be, a 1280px variant
	served every viewport up to 1919px — every 1366 to 1536px laptop — and
	upscaled it. Each query is a closed range here, because these are `media`
	attributes on four separate links: an open-ended
	`media="(min-width: 640px)"` would match three queries at once on a wide
	screen and preload the whole ladder.

	Without an uploaded photo (masthead_image is empty) this renders only the
	preloads of the static banner, which is what styles.css falls back to: that
	is also the background of the error pages.

	`error_page` is set by not_found(). The error pages paint a plain
	gradient (`.masthead.error-masthead`) and share the art in error_art.twig
	instead of a photo, so both branches below would only preload an image
	nobody paints — which costs the visitor the bytes without earning the
	paint.

	The |raw filters below are required, not sloppiness: <style> is a raw text
	element, so the HTML parser hands its content to CSS undecoded. Without
	them the escaped ampersand of the /picture query string would end up in the
	css url() literally and the hero would 404. The href attributes above take
	the escaped form, which is what an attribute value wants.
#}
{% if error_page is not defined %}
	{% if masthead_image is defined and masthead_image is not empty %}
		<link rel="preload" as="image" href="{{ masthead_image.small }}" media="(max-width: 639.98px)" fetchpriority="high"/>
		<link rel="preload" as="image" href="{{ masthead_image.medium }}" media="(min-width: 640px) and (max-width: 1279.98px)" fetchpriority="high"/>
		<link rel="preload" as="image" href="{{ masthead_image.wide }}" media="(min-width: 1280px) and (max-width: 1919.98px)" fetchpriority="high"/>
		<link rel="preload" as="image" href="{{ masthead_image.large }}" media="(min-width: 1920px)" fetchpriority="high"/>
		<style>
			.masthead {
				--masthead-image-small: url('{{ masthead_image.small|raw }}');
				--masthead-image-medium: url('{{ masthead_image.medium|raw }}');
				--masthead-image-wide: url('{{ masthead_image.wide|raw }}');
				--masthead-image-large: url('{{ masthead_image.large|raw }}');
			}
		</style>
	{% else %}
		<link rel="preload" as="image" href="/caving-banner-tiny.webp" media="(max-width: 639.98px)" fetchpriority="high"/>
		<link rel="preload" as="image" href="/caving-banner-mid.webp" media="(min-width: 640px) and (max-width: 1279.98px)" fetchpriority="high"/>
		<link rel="preload" as="image" href="/caving-banner-wide.webp" media="(min-width: 1280px) and (max-width: 1919.98px)" fetchpriority="high"/>
		<link rel="preload" as="image" href="/caving-banner.webp" media="(min-width: 1920px)" fetchpriority="high"/>
	{% endif %}
{% endif %}